# i18n Rules

The game is English-only. `en-US` is the only locale and the source of truth; the language registry is `static/locales/registry.json` (default/fallback/schema locale).

1. **Edit module sources, not build products**: when a new feature, item, or UI needs user-visible strings, add or edit them in `static/locales/en-US/modules/*.po` and `static/locales/en-US/game_configs_modules/*.po`. These are the maintained sources. `static/locales/en-US/LC_MESSAGES/messages.po` and `static/locales/en-US/LC_MESSAGES/game_configs.po` are merged build products generated by `python tools/i18n/build_mo.py`; do not edit `LC_MESSAGES/*.po` directly (unless you are explicitly fixing the build script), or the next build will overwrite your changes.
2. **Rebuild after editing sources**: after changing any split `.po` source file, run `python tools/i18n/build_mo.py` so that `LC_MESSAGES/*.po` / `.mo` stay consistent with the sources.
3. **Frontend strings**: frontend UI strings live under `web/src/locales/en-US/`.
4. **`msgid` uses English source text or stable keys**: a `msgid` in a `.po` file must be English source text or a stable key such as `feature_xxx_label` or `tribulation_inner_demon`.
5. **Races and yao effects are a cross-stack i18n contract**: when adding or changing `static/game_configs/race.csv`, yao actions, yao effect keys, or race options in character creation, also update the backend `game_configs_modules/race.po` / `modules/race.po` / `modules/yao_actions.po` and the frontend creation panel display. The backend provides localized structured DTOs; the frontend must not hardcode user-visible race labels (e.g. Human/Fox/Wolf/Bird/Snake/Turtle).
6. **Runtime-generated text is handled separately from UI translation**: LLM/runtime-generated text such as `backstory`, `thinking`, and goals is not translated with the UI. When adding generated-text constraints or prompt fragments, go through locale templates (`static/locales/en-US/templates/*.txt`) or translation keys; never hardcode natural-language text in Python logic as final user-visible content.
7. **Short slots stay concise**: `title`, `label`, `tab`, `button`, `badge`, `status`, `*_short`, menu items, status bar entries, and card titles should use short, natural wording without losing meaning. Put full explanations in `*_desc` / `help` keys (add a separate short/long key pair when both are needed) instead of letting one long string serve every context.
8. **Adding a language in the future**: start by registering it in `static/locales/registry.json`, then scaffold the directories, scripts, and resources. Tools under `tools/i18n/` read the registry; never hardcode locale lists.
